<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · river</p><h1 class="enc-title">Qiantang River</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Qiantang River is the main river of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zhejiang">Zhejiang</a> province in eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a>, flowing past <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hangzhou">Hangzhou</a> into Hangzhou Bay and the East China Sea. Its funnel-shaped estuary produces the Qiantang tidal bore, one of the largest in the world. From the 10th century the Wuyue kingdom built stone sea walls along its banks, and Hangzhou, once called Qiantang, grew on its northern shore.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/qiantang-river.jpg" alt="Qiantang River" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: David290 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Qiantang_River_Bridge_DJI_0575_(2).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
